  "text": " The most common email I get is, and I'm wide open by the way, my cell phone is all over the internet, my email is over the internet, and I get emails from all over. Just bring it on. I can't answer them all, but I'll do the best I can. I get the email, Dr. McCullough, I'm going to lose my job, all capital letters, my job. If I don't take the vaccine, say, well, about half of America is going to lose their job if they don't take the vaccine. But of course, it's their job. Then my response is, well, what's the social contract? Are you going to get three months of work? Do you get six months of work? Are you getting 20 years of employment? Do you know what you're getting from your employment perspective? No, I'm just going to lose my job. Wait a minute. You're going to lose your job. You don't even know if you get it. How much employment you get out of this? You don't even know what the deal is. You're just being told to take a vaccine. So one of my favorite vignettes is, I text him all the time, he's been texting me this morning, it's pharmacist from Kaiser. He goes, I'm going to lose my job. I said, well, fill out these exemptions, and he filled out these exemptions. He submits it to the vaccine office. And then 10 minutes later, he goes, we regret to inform you, your exemptions have been declined. And then he emails back and he says, he goes, is this the same office that I have my attorney contact you for a letter of intent to file suit for harassment? And then 10 minutes later, we're happy to accept your exemptions. This is the biggest game of chicken being played of all time. And let's see some backbone on this. Really? Come on.",
